  {
   "id": "fn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1070,
   "y": 1244,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100093,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700651,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Not warming up and not idle - fully caught up at ALL TIMES, processing every event\nthe primary does and maintaining a byte-identical book. Which works only because\nmatching is deterministic: same inputs, same sequence, therefore same state.\n\nPrimary and standby differ in exactly ONE thing: whether they publish. Both\ncompute; one speaks. So promotion is not a state transfer - it is a flag flip, and\nit completes in the time it takes to detect the failure.",
   "originalText": "Not warming up and not idle - fully caught up at ALL TIMES, processing every event\nthe primary does and maintaining a byte-identical book. Which works only because\nmatching is deterministic: same inputs, same sequence, therefore same state.\n\nPrimary and standby differ in exactly ONE thing: whether they publish. Both\ncompute; one speaks. So promotion is not a state transfer - it is a flag flip, and\nit completes in the time it takes to detect the failure.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fen",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1400,
   "width": 785,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100094,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700658,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Fencing - because the failure that matters is a primary that APPEARS dead and is not",
   "originalText": "Fencing - because the failure that matters is a primary that APPEARS dead and is not",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fen2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1426,
   "width": 737,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100095,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700665,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A GC pause, a partition or a slow disk makes a healthy primary miss heartbeats. Promote the\nstandby, the old primary resumes publishing, and now TWO engines publish conflicting fills\nfor the same orders - both internally consistent, and unreconcilable. So leadership is a\nLEASE WITH AN EPOCH: every published event carries (epoch, sequence), consumers track the\nhighest epoch seen and REJECT anything lower, and a promotion increments it.",
   "originalText": "A GC pause, a partition or a slow disk makes a healthy primary miss heartbeats. Promote the\nstandby, the old primary resumes publishing, and now TWO engines publish conflicting fills\nfor the same orders - both internally consistent, and unreconcilable. So leadership is a\nLEASE WITH AN EPOCH: every published event carries (epoch, sequence), consumers track the\nhighest epoch seen and REJECT anything lower, and a promotion increments it.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fen3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1070,
   "y": 1426,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 97,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100096,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700672,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A deposed primary keeps processing into its own memory harmlessly - it\nsimply cannot be heard. Same pattern as the message queue's leader_epoch\nand the wallet's phase-status CAS, and the reason is always identical:\n'I am the leader' is a claim that EXPIRES, and a monotonic epoch is what\nmakes expiry checkable by the RECIPIENT rather than trusted from the\nclaimant.",
   "originalText": "A deposed primary keeps processing into its own memory harmlessly - it\nsimply cannot be heard. Same pattern as the message queue's leader_epoch\nand the wallet's phase-status CAS, and the reason is always identical:\n'I am the leader' is a claim that EXPIRES, and a monotonic epoch is what\nmakes expiry checkable by the RECIPIENT rather than trusted from the\nclaimant.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
