   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100114,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700798,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "deliberate unavailability",
   "originalText": "deliberate unavailability",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1750,
   "width": 979,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100115,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700805,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "That last row is the design's most important reliability decision. Halting a symbol is embarrassing, publicly visible and\ncosts money. Publishing two divergent books means fills that do not reconcile and positions that do not exist - and it is\nUNFIXABLE AFTER THE FACT, because you cannot un-tell a broker that their order filled. When you cannot be sure who is\nauthoritative, being UNAVAILABLE is strictly better than being WRONG.",
   "originalText": "That last row is the design's most important reliability decision. Halting a symbol is embarrassing, publicly visible and\ncosts money. Publishing two divergent books means fills that do not reconcile and positions that do not exist - and it is\nUNFIXABLE AFTER THE FACT, because you cannot un-tell a broker that their order filled. When you cannot be sure who is\nauthoritative, being UNAVAILABLE is strictly better than being WRONG.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1030,
   "y": 1750,
   "width": 560,
   "height": 146,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100116,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700812,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why not multi-region: a cross-region round trip is 150 ms, four\norders of magnitude over the budget - but the deeper objection is\nconceptual. An exchange IS a single authoritative ordering of events\nper symbol, and that is precisely what geographic distribution cannot\nprovide. Two regions accepting orders independently produce two\norderings, and reconciling them means deciding retroactively whose\ntrades happened. So DR is a standby datacenter for resuming after a\ncatastrophe, never active-active - and a regional disaster means a\ntrading halt.",
   "originalText": "Why not multi-region: a cross-region round trip is 150 ms, four\norders of magnitude over the budget - but the deeper objection is\nconceptual. An exchange IS a single authoritative ordering of events\nper symbol, and that is precisely what geographic distribution cannot\nprovide. Two regions accepting orders independently produce two\norderings, and reconciling them means deciding retroactively whose\ntrades happened. So DR is a standby datacenter for resuming after a\ncatastrophe, never active-active - and a regional disaster means a\ntrading halt.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1842,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100117,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700819,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the honest gap: colocation sells the right to be physically closer to the multicast source, partially undoing this\nmodule's fairness work. The defence - stated as a defence, not as fairness - is that the advantage is BOUNDED (metres of\ncable, not unbounded software), OPENLY PRICED (anyone can buy it) and DISCLOSED, unlike the unicast loop's invisible,\nunpriced advantage determined by an arbitrary iteration order. Better, and not the same thing as simultaneous delivery.",
   "originalText": "And the honest gap: colocation sells the right to be physically closer to the multicast source, partially undoing this\nmodule's fairness work. The defence - stated as a defence, not as fairness - is that the advantage is BOUNDED (metres of\ncable, not unbounded software), OPENLY PRICED (anyone can buy it) and DISCLOSED, unlike the unicast loop's invisible,\nunpriced advantage determined by an arbitrary iteration order. Better, and not the same thing as simultaneous delivery.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
